I'll complete the requested file change.

The code has a bug: when flattening with recursion, it passes `depth` unchanged instead of decrementing it. This means every nested level gets flattened to the same depth instead of going one level deeper each time.

Additionally, the code needs to validate that `depth` is a non-negative integer or `Infinity`, and that `items` is an array.

```json
{"action": "write_file", "path": "flatten.js", "content": "'use strict';

function flatten(items, depth = 1) {
  // Validate items
  if (!Array.isArray(items)) {
    throw new TypeError('items must be an array');
  }

  // Validate depth
  if (
    depth !== Infinity &&
    (typeof depth !== 'number' ||
      !Number.isInteger(depth) ||
      depth < 0 ||
      Number.isNaN(depth))
  ) {
    throw new RangeError('depth must be a non-negative integer or Infinity');
  }

  const out = [];
  for (const item of items) {
    if (Array.isArray(item) && depth > 0) {
      out.push(...flatten(item, depth - 1));
    } else {
      out.push(item);
    }
  }
  return out;
}

module.exports = { flatten };
"}
```

